  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment must establish a reliable baseline for the multimodal setting. config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) uses the most standard and well-validated components: ResNet50 as a robust image encoder, scVI-200 as a standard single-cell RNA encoder, multiprofile to leverage profile diversity, simple avgpool aggregation, and weighted fusion to let the model learn modality importance. This 'central' configuration tests the core hypothesis that combining image and RNA modalities improves accuracy. Its result will anchor all subsequent comparisons: if it performs well, later experiments can exploit by swapping individual components (e.g., ViT-L, scGPT, transformer aggregation); if it underperforms, single-modality baselines (experiments 2-3) can isolate which component is the bottleneck. This maximizes information gain per experiment under a tight 10-experiment budget."
}

